          %hr/
          %h1#20090630 2009-06-30
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+object"} Eilenberg-MacLane object
                    prompted by the blog discussion
                    %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/06/cohomology_and_homotopy.html#c024902"} here
                %li
                  %p
                    replied at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"}> Toby Bartels
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  Responded to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"} Ronnie Brown
                  at
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
                %li
                  Noted an incomplete thought at
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy"} simplicial homotopy
                %li
                  Complained a bit at
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
                %li
                  %p
                    added definition to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
                %li
                  %p
                    reorganized
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p expanded the idea/introduction-section
                    %li
                      %p moved the original material to
                      %ul
                        %li
                          %p
                            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} global model structure on simplicial presheaves
                            (and expanded that)
                        %li
                          %p
                            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
                    %li
                      %p
                        created
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} local model structure on simplicial sheaves
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rectified+infinity-stack"} rectified infinity-stack
                %li
                  %p
                    fixed (hopefully) the nonsense paragraph (due to me) that
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"} Toby
                    had pointed out at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"}> Tim
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    I have pointed out at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy"} simplicial homotopy
                    that the combinatorial description has much greater validity than claimed there before. It works for simplicial objects in any finitely cocomplete category. (I think that is in Duskin’s Memoir volume, but is not difficult to check directly.) It depends on having the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} copower
                    with
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[1]
                %li
                  %p
                    We have two notations for simplices in
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi SSet
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
                    and
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
                      that
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
                      is due to me – I’ll try to change it back to
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
                      (same for horns) where I see it
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    prompted by
                    = succeed "\u2018s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"} David
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
                    I was led to all of the following:
                  %p
                    I split
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                    into
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+%28as+a+transformation%29"} homotopy (as a transformation)
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+%28as+an+operation%29"} homotopy (as an operation)
                  %p
                    and moved the material originally found at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                    to
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+%28as+a+transformation%29"} homotopy (as a transformation)
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                    and then wrote
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+%28as+an+operation%29"} homotopy (as an operation)
                    in the spirit of David’s remark and in the light of the entry
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckmann-Hilton+duality"} Eckmann-Hilton duality
                    (but just some tentative abstract nonsense so far).
                  %p
                    then finally I added to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
                    a last section “some abstract nonsense” that indicates how the discussion of homtopy groups could be given analogous, just dual, to the discussion the way we have it (since recently) at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} cohomology group
                %li
                  %p
                    expanded at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} cohomology group
                    (standard abelian examples, standard nonabelian examples)
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"} David Corfield
                      has an interesting question there, I think he is right, will try to write something at
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"} David
              %ul
                %li
                  added to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckmann-Hilton+duality"} Eckmann-Hilton duality
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    continued polishing and adding statements and proofs to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
                %li
